# SAMBO

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines the physiological, biomechanical, technical and tactical demands of Sambo.

Its purpose is to enable the Combat Athlete System (CAS) to understand the unique performance profile of Sambo athletes and to individualize physical preparation accordingly.

This document describes performance requirements.

It does not prescribe training methods.

---

# Definition

Sambo is a grappling combat sport originating from Eastern Europe, combining wrestling and judo techniques with a unique emphasis on dynamic throws, leg attacks and lower-limb submissions.

Combat Sambo additionally integrates striking.

This document focuses primarily on **Sport Sambo**, while identifying specific adaptations required for Combat Sambo.

---

# Philosophy

Sambo rewards continuous initiative.

Athletes constantly transition between standing exchanges and ground fighting while seeking opportunities for throws, positional control and submissions.

Efficiency, explosiveness and adaptability are equally important.

The objective is to dominate transitions before dominating positions.

